node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.vite/
.chrome-profile-*/
storybook-static/

# Next 16 writes these on every dev start ("Generated AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md for AI agents"); the repo guidance lives in the root CLAUDE.md.
apps/docs/AGENTS.md
apps/docs/CLAUDE.md

# agent scratch hosts and captures, never tracked
.scratch/
.scratch-host/
# Agent scratch — machine-local. Repo guidance lives in CLAUDE.md, which is tracked.
.claude/
# ...except the feedback ledger: CLAUDE.md @-imports it, so it has to travel
# with a clone or a worktree rather than staying on one machine (rate skill,
# "Leave the trace in the repo too").
!.claude/
!.claude/feedback.md
# ...and settings.json's worktree.baseRef: CLAUDE.md's own "Isolated agent
# lanes" section calls it load-bearing for every lane in THIS repo — without
# it a fresh worktree branches from origin/main and can't see the branch it
# was cut from (measured 2026-09-17, P9c). It's a repo invariant, not a
# per-machine preference, so unlike most of .claude/ it travels with a
# clone/worktree rather than needing every checkout to reinvent it. If this
# file ever grows machine-local content (personal permission allowlists,
# local model overrides), split those into a second, still-ignored file
# rather than un-tracking this one.
!.claude/settings.json
# wrangler local state
.wrangler/
# Reports: the page is tracked, the captures it inlines are not (Zach, 2026-09-07).
reports/media/
# Python bytecode from scripts/ (the desktop launcher writes this on every run).
__pycache__/
